     "answer": "1) An alloy is a homogeneous mixture of a metal with other metals or non-metals, prepared mainly to improve hardness, strength, lustre and resistance to corrosion. 2) Brass is copper plus zinc, used for utensils and decorative articles. 3) Bronze is copper plus tin, used for statues, medals and bells because it is hard and resists corrosion. 4) Solder is lead plus tin, with a low melting point, used for welding electrical wires together. 5) Stainless steel is iron with chromium and nickel, used for utensils and surgical instruments because it does not rust. 6) Pure metals are often too soft or corrode easily; alloying with suitable elements gives the required hardness, durability and resistance, and also lowers the melting point where needed, as in solder."
