     "answer": "The pH scale measures the acidity or basicity of a solution, ranging from 0 to 14. pH < 7 indicates acidic, pH = 7 is neutral, and pH > 7 is basic. The pH is calculated as pH = -log[H+], where [H+] is the hydrogen ion concentration. Importance: 1) Determines the suitability of water for various purposes. 2) Controls chemical reactions in industrial processes. 3) Essential for biological processes. (a) Pure water has pH 7 (neutral). (b) Lemon juice is acidic with pH around 2-3 due to citric acid content."
